title: script:stop
tags: [[GUI command]] [[Scripting the GUI]]
kind: reference
summary: Ask the running script to stop (the one asking, by default)

Asks a script the GUI started to stop: `SIGTERM` to its whole process group, which a script may trap to finish what it is doing. Without an argument, the script asking the current question — what Escape does while a question is up; with a run id (`script-3`), that one. Once the script is gone the GUI closes the workspaces it opened and gives their slots back. A script that ignores the signal goes on: <<cmd "script:kill">> ends it. A question nobody owns is closed instead ([[Script sessions]]).
